1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,540
Once upon a time, there was a princess raised by loving parents.

2
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:14,780
One day, the princess snuck past the guard of the gate and slipped out of the castle for the very first time.

3
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:23,920
No matter how far she went, however, outside the castle there was only an endless forest as black as pitch.

4
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:31,800
Before she knew it, the princess ended up unable to either escape the forest or return to the castle.

5
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:37,780
In that kingdom, the inside of the castle was the entire world.

6
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:35,479
MUTO

7
00:02:39,479 --> 00:02:44,479
Bakir cast down his sword and found something only he could do.

8
00:02:44,479 --> 00:02:45,479
I want to protect him.

9
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:47,479
Because he wants to help MUTO.

10
00:02:47,479 --> 00:02:50,479
The pure-hearted MUTO who's always risked himself.

11
00:02:50,479 --> 00:02:54,479
Never giving up, no matter how much he's hurt.

12
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:58,479
Overcoming the painful memories he wants to forget.

13
00:03:01,479 --> 00:03:03,479
Bakir is strong.

14
00:03:03,479 --> 00:03:05,479
Even if he's not carrying a sword,

15
00:03:05,479 --> 00:03:07,479
Bakir is MUTO's knight.

16
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:09,479
What's Bakir doing, Sora?

17
00:03:09,479 --> 00:03:11,479
He's talking to the oak tree,

18
00:03:11,479 --> 00:03:15,479
so he can write a story that protects the person who's important to him.

19
00:03:15,479 --> 00:03:19,479
Maybe Bakir really doesn't need help from anyone

20
00:03:19,479 --> 00:03:22,479
and can protect MUTO all by himself.

21
00:03:22,479 --> 00:03:25,479
Can you really say you love me?

22
00:03:27,479 --> 00:03:31,479
Does MUTO's heart just keep getting more and more stained by the raven's blood?

23
00:03:31,479 --> 00:03:33,479
So that he's mean even to Rue?

24
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:35,479
Poor Rue.

25
00:03:35,479 --> 00:03:37,479
I'm kinda worried about her.

26
00:03:37,479 --> 00:03:39,479
I still can't do anything helpful though.

27
00:03:39,479 --> 00:03:40,479
Hmm.

28
00:03:40,479 --> 00:03:41,479
Duck?

29
00:03:41,479 --> 00:03:42,479
Huh?

30
00:03:42,479 --> 00:03:43,479
Are you okay, Sora?

31
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:44,479
Huh?

32
00:03:44,479 --> 00:03:46,479
Are you worrying about me?

33
00:03:46,479 --> 00:03:47,479
Thank you.

34
00:03:47,479 --> 00:03:49,479
Don't worry, I'm okay.

35
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:50,479
Oh good, Sora.

36
00:03:50,479 --> 00:03:53,479
I thought the teacher might get mad at you, Sora.

37
00:03:53,479 --> 00:03:54,479
What?

38
00:03:54,479 --> 00:03:56,479
You're skipping school with Bakir, Sora!

39
00:03:56,479 --> 00:03:57,479
Ah!

40
00:03:57,479 --> 00:03:58,479
Ah!

41
00:03:58,479 --> 00:04:01,479
Oh no, I came here thinking I'd check on Bakir on my way to school,

42
00:04:01,479 --> 00:04:02,479
but it's this late already!

43
00:04:02,479 --> 00:04:03,479
Huh?

44
00:04:03,479 --> 00:04:04,479
Yeah, sorry!

45
00:04:04,479 --> 00:04:05,479
Come on, Uzzuru, let's get going!

46
00:04:05,479 --> 00:04:07,479
Okay, Uzzuru, see you later!

47
