66
00:04:26,479 --> 00:04:27,479
Ah!

67
00:04:27,479 --> 00:04:28,479
Ah!

68
00:04:28,479 --> 00:04:29,479
Ah!

69
00:04:29,479 --> 00:04:30,479
What?

70
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:33,479
Rue, why is she...

71
00:04:33,479 --> 00:04:34,479
...Uzzura?

72
00:04:35,479 --> 00:04:36,479
Wow!

73
00:04:36,479 --> 00:04:37,279
It's open!

74
00:04:50,239 --> 00:04:50,719
Rue!

75
00:04:52,139 --> 00:04:52,659
Tutu.

76
00:04:52,899 --> 00:04:54,339
Were you just crying?

77
00:04:54,839 --> 00:04:55,559
Of course not.

78
00:04:55,759 --> 00:04:56,559
What are you doing here?

79
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,019
It seemed like you were acting a little strange.

80
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:01,119
Well, really strange.

81
00:05:01,179 --> 00:05:02,839
Anyway, I mean, this is really dangerous.

82
00:05:03,519 --> 00:05:03,999
Dangerous?

83
00:05:04,539 --> 00:05:05,579
Why would it be?

84
00:05:05,579 --> 00:05:07,579
As you know, I am Cray-hee.

85
00:05:09,239 --> 00:05:10,139
You're Rue!

86
00:05:10,739 --> 00:05:11,979
That's who you are!

87
00:05:12,539 --> 00:05:14,859
That's how I think of you!

88
00:05:15,639 --> 00:05:16,279
I mean...

89
00:05:16,279 --> 00:05:18,919
That scared me.

90
00:05:19,119 --> 00:05:20,699
I'd say you're the one in danger.

91
00:05:20,959 --> 00:05:22,599
Yeah, sure looks that way, huh?

92
00:05:23,519 --> 00:05:24,579
I'm still...

93
00:05:28,579 --> 00:05:31,419
I'm still Princess Cray-hee regardless.

94
00:05:31,419 --> 00:05:38,039
B-B-B-Rue.

95
00:05:44,539 --> 00:05:45,039
Doug!

96
00:05:45,039 --> 00:05:47,199
Where the heck were you?

97
00:05:47,199 --> 00:05:47,979
You're awful!

98
00:05:47,979 --> 00:05:48,519
Huh?

99
00:05:48,519 --> 00:05:49,979
Poor, poor dad!

100
00:05:49,979 --> 00:05:50,639
Dad!

101
00:05:50,639 --> 00:05:53,359
I can't believe you would actually skip point class!

102
00:05:53,359 --> 00:05:54,859
Oh, well, you see...

103
00:05:54,859 --> 00:05:55,859
He's coming!

104
00:05:55,859 --> 00:05:56,859
He's coming!

105
00:05:56,859 --> 00:05:59,259
Don't be scared!

106
00:05:59,259 --> 00:06:00,059
That's scary!

107
00:06:00,539 --> 00:06:02,839
Now, Duck, just wriggle your way out of it.

108
00:06:03,079 --> 00:06:04,139
It's your one hope!

109
00:06:04,139 --> 00:06:04,639
Huh?

110
00:06:04,639 --> 00:06:05,139
Out of what?

111
00:06:05,139 --> 00:06:05,639
He's here!

112
00:06:05,639 --> 00:06:06,819
So, he's come!

113
00:06:06,819 --> 00:06:15,399
So, Miss Duck, it's time we both had a little talk.

114
00:06:15,399 --> 00:06:18,619
It's finally the pro-posal.

115
00:06:18,619 --> 00:06:19,439
What?

116
00:06:19,439 --> 00:06:21,939
Here, Duck, I'll hold your books for you.

117
00:06:21,939 --> 00:06:23,519
Um, uh, thank you.

118
00:06:23,519 --> 00:06:25,699
Now get out there and start wriggling.

119
00:06:25,699 --> 00:06:27,439
Yeah, uh, right.

120
00:06:27,439 --> 00:06:29,159
Miss Duck.

121
00:06:29,159 --> 00:06:30,059
Yes, sir?

122
00:06:30,059 --> 00:06:35,699
Everybody has times when they feel as if they'll never be able to reach their dreams.

123
00:06:35,699 --> 00:06:37,119
Huh?

124
00:06:37,119 --> 00:06:42,199
However, deciding there's no way you can do something is nothing more than a way of comforting

125
00:06:42,199 --> 00:06:45,899
yourself when you lack motivation.

126
00:06:45,899 --> 00:06:49,899
Are you positive you're not fooling yourself about how you feel?

127
00:06:49,899 --> 00:06:54,399
About what is exactly the most important thing to you in the whole world?

128
00:06:54,399 --> 00:07:02,699
I decided to become a girl for Mewtwo, and I became Princess Tutu for Mewtwo.

129
00:07:02,699 --> 00:07:09,199
But somewhere, somehow, I came to the conclusion that I couldn't do anything.

130
00:07:09,199 --> 00:07:11,199
Am I running away?

131
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:12,899
What's most important to me?

132
00:07:12,899 --> 00:07:18,619
So, if perchance this dream you've been suppressing far too long is to marry me, and your heart isn't

133
00:07:18,619 --> 00:07:23,619
in your lessons because you're agonizing over that, and I, for my part, must reserve a place

134
00:07:23,619 --> 00:07:25,119
to hold the ceremony in once.

135
00:07:25,119 --> 00:07:26,119
Ah!

136
00:07:26,119 --> 00:07:28,119
Thank you for all your help, Mr. Cat.

137
00:07:28,119 --> 00:07:29,119
Goodbye, now.

138
00:07:29,119 --> 00:07:30,119
Goodbye.

139
00:07:30,119 --> 00:07:31,119
Ah!

140
00:07:31,119 --> 00:07:32,119
She squirmed out of it.

141
00:07:32,119 --> 00:07:35,119
It's a big shock for Mr. Cat.

142
00:07:35,119 --> 00:07:37,119
I can't let things stay this way.

143
00:07:37,119 --> 00:07:39,119
I'll search for the heart chart.

144
00:07:39,119 --> 00:07:40,119
I'll search the town.

145
00:07:40,119 --> 00:07:42,619
That's what I can do right now!

146
00:07:42,619 --> 00:07:44,619
It's what I can do for Mewtwo!

147
00:07:54,619 --> 00:07:56,619
Are you the ruler worried about Zora?

148
00:07:56,619 --> 00:07:57,619
What?

149
00:07:57,619 --> 00:07:59,619
Duck said that, Zora!

150
00:07:59,619 --> 00:08:00,619
What?

151
00:08:00,619 --> 00:08:01,619
Duck did?

152
00:08:01,619 --> 00:08:04,119
I already told you there is no Rue.

153
00:08:04,119 --> 00:08:05,119
That's not true!

154
00:08:05,119 --> 00:08:07,119
I don't believe that!

155
00:08:07,119 --> 00:08:11,119
I get this feeling you're still Rue!

156
00:08:11,119 --> 00:08:12,119
You're Rue!

157
00:08:14,119 --> 00:08:15,119
Have I?

158
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:17,119
Have I met you somewhere before, Zora?

159
00:08:17,119 --> 00:08:18,119
What do you mean?

160
00:08:18,119 --> 00:08:20,119
I've never met a girl like…

161
00:08:22,119 --> 00:08:25,119
Who… are you?

162
00:08:25,119 --> 00:08:26,119
Uzzra!

163
00:08:26,119 --> 00:08:27,119
Is Uzzra Zora?

164
00:08:27,119 --> 00:08:28,119
So do…

165
00:08:28,119 --> 00:08:30,119
Do you actually know…

166
00:08:30,119 --> 00:08:33,619
Do you know if I'm really the Crows?

167
00:08:35,619 --> 00:08:36,619
This is stupid.

168
00:08:36,619 --> 00:08:39,619
I don't have time for this nonsense.

169
00:08:40,619 --> 00:08:42,619
This is some sort of mistake!

170
00:08:43,619 --> 00:08:45,619
Sure, when I investigated Drosselmeyer's family tree,

171
00:08:45,619 --> 00:08:47,619
he was a direct descendant.

172
00:08:47,619 --> 00:08:49,619
But he was only able to find that out

173
00:08:49,619 --> 00:08:52,619
thanks to my taking note of him and showing him myself.

174
00:08:52,619 --> 00:08:55,619
I even know who you people are!

175
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,619
I am far more qualified.

176
00:08:58,619 --> 00:09:01,119
I want you people to acknowledge me.

177
00:09:01,119 --> 00:09:03,119
You who are the stoppers of stories.

178
00:09:03,119 --> 00:09:05,119
The so-called bookmen.

179
00:09:05,119 --> 00:09:08,119
There aren't any qualifications to being human.

180
00:09:08,119 --> 00:09:09,119
That's not my point!

181
00:09:09,119 --> 00:09:13,119
Is this world under the control of Drosselmeyer's stories or not?

182
00:09:13,119 --> 00:09:15,119
Whether living in this world hinders our discernment

183
00:09:15,119 --> 00:09:16,119
doesn't matter to me.

184
00:09:16,119 --> 00:09:19,119
I want to know the truth of this mystery.

185
00:09:19,119 --> 00:09:21,119
There are things it's okay to know

186
00:09:21,119 --> 00:09:23,119
and things that it's not.

187
00:09:23,119 --> 00:09:24,119
Go home.

188
00:09:24,119 --> 00:09:25,619
Damn it.

189
00:09:37,619 --> 00:09:40,619
Let's cut that boy's hands off too.

190
00:09:40,619 --> 00:09:43,619
Just like we did to Drosselmeyer.

191
00:09:43,619 --> 00:09:46,619
Let's cut them off before he starts writing stories.

192
00:09:46,619 --> 00:09:47,619
Patience.

193
00:09:47,619 --> 00:09:50,119
As bookmen, our time is too precious

194
00:09:50,119 --> 00:09:54,119
to be wasting it on fighting false storytellers.

195
00:09:54,119 --> 00:09:58,119
Then let's get the one who exchanges words with the oak tree.

196
00:10:00,119 --> 00:10:02,119
What on earth am I doing?

197
00:10:02,119 --> 00:10:05,119
Father is seeking a heart, and yet I…

198
00:10:05,119 --> 00:10:07,119
Damn it!

199
00:10:07,119 --> 00:10:09,119
So Fakir, he's the one, is he?

200
00:10:09,119 --> 00:10:11,119
Then what was I born into this world for?

201
00:10:11,119 --> 00:10:12,119
What would…

202
00:10:15,119 --> 00:10:16,619
It's so cold.

203
00:10:18,619 --> 00:10:19,619
What's wrong?

204
00:10:21,619 --> 00:10:24,619
You're Rue from the ballet division.

205
00:10:25,619 --> 00:10:26,619
Huh?

206
00:10:26,619 --> 00:10:45,119
Somewhere in this town.

207
00:10:45,119 --> 00:10:47,119
There's gotta be a heart joint somewhere.

208
00:10:51,119 --> 00:10:52,119
Quack!

209
00:10:54,119 --> 00:10:55,619
Who's there?

210
00:10:56,619 --> 00:11:00,119
Just now Mewto's shadow looked like a crow.

211
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:03,119
Be careful, little duck.

212
00:11:03,119 --> 00:11:06,119
Because for the stoppers of story,

213
00:11:06,119 --> 00:11:09,619
beheading a defenseless little duck

214
00:11:09,619 --> 00:11:12,119
is mere child's prey.

215
00:11:12,119 --> 00:11:14,119
Ho, ho, ho, ho.

216
00:11:26,619 --> 00:11:28,119
What should I do?

217
00:11:28,119 --> 00:11:29,119
What?

218
00:11:29,119 --> 00:11:30,119
What?

219
00:11:30,119 --> 00:11:31,119
What?

220
00:11:31,119 --> 00:11:33,119
Say, what happened to all the other birds?

221
00:11:33,119 --> 00:11:35,119
They just won't come when I call them.

222
00:11:35,119 --> 00:11:36,119
Mewto?

223
00:11:36,119 --> 00:11:37,119
What?

224
00:11:37,119 --> 00:11:38,119
Strange, isn't it?

225
00:11:38,119 --> 00:11:53,619
When here, I love everyone in the world and want to protect them.

226
00:11:53,619 --> 00:11:55,119
The prince's heart.

227
00:11:55,119 --> 00:11:59,119
But I also want to make all the world's love my own.

228
00:12:01,119 --> 00:12:03,119
I wonder which is the real me.

229
00:12:03,119 --> 00:12:04,619
I want people to love me.

230
00:12:04,619 --> 00:12:05,619
I want people to love me.

231
00:12:05,619 --> 00:12:07,619
But is it okay to just be loved?

232
00:12:07,619 --> 00:12:09,119
I don't know.

233
00:12:09,119 --> 00:12:11,119
My pride is still lost in the dark.

234
00:12:13,119 --> 00:12:16,119
I must overcome this raven's blood in me

235
00:12:16,119 --> 00:12:18,119
and uphold my pride as a prince.

236
00:12:18,119 --> 00:12:21,119
It is my duty to protect all the people.

237
00:12:24,119 --> 00:12:26,119
I want my heart to be whole soon.

238
00:12:26,119 --> 00:12:28,619
Quack, Mewto.

239
00:12:28,619 --> 00:12:31,619
Once I have all the shards of my heart back.

240
00:12:37,619 --> 00:12:39,619
I'm sorry, Mewto.

241
00:12:39,619 --> 00:12:41,619
I swore to get all of your heart back,

242
00:12:41,619 --> 00:12:43,619
but I'm sorry.

243
00:12:43,619 --> 00:12:45,619
I'm going to do my best.

244
00:12:45,619 --> 00:12:47,619
They must be somewhere in this town.

245
00:12:47,619 --> 00:12:49,619
I will find them.

246
00:12:49,619 --> 00:12:50,619
I will.

247
00:12:50,619 --> 00:12:52,619
I'll certainly, definitely,

248
00:12:52,619 --> 00:12:55,619
absolutely, positively find them.

249
00:12:55,619 --> 00:12:57,619
Because that's all I can do.

250
00:13:03,619 --> 00:13:05,619
I can feel your heart beating.

251
00:13:05,619 --> 00:13:07,119
It's rather fast.

252
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:08,119
Why is that?

253
00:13:08,119 --> 00:13:11,119
Because you're so fragrant.

254
00:13:16,619 --> 00:13:18,119
Come with me.

255
00:13:19,119 --> 00:13:20,119
Okay.

256
00:13:25,619 --> 00:13:26,619
Who are you?

257
00:13:26,619 --> 00:13:27,619
We are the Bookmen.

258
00:13:27,619 --> 00:13:29,619
If you intend to employ Drosselmeyer's power

259
00:13:29,619 --> 00:13:30,619
to spin stories yourself,

260
00:13:30,619 --> 00:13:31,619
we will be forced to stop you.

261
00:13:31,619 --> 00:13:32,619
The Bookmen?

262
00:13:32,619 --> 00:13:33,619
Our ancestors cut off Drosselmeyer's hands

263
00:13:33,619 --> 00:13:39,619
and made him unable to spin stories ever again.

264
00:13:39,619 --> 00:13:41,619
Should his descendant ever try to spin a story,

265
00:13:41,619 --> 00:13:43,619
we must deal him the same fate.

266
00:13:43,619 --> 00:13:50,619
That is the duty that has been passed down to us over generations.

267
00:13:50,619 --> 00:13:51,619
So you're going to cut off my hands then?

268
00:13:51,619 --> 00:13:53,619
Dangerous stories must not be born.

269
00:13:53,619 --> 00:13:55,619
Dangerous stories must not be born.

270
00:13:55,619 --> 00:13:56,619
We must stop the stories that already have been born

271
00:13:56,619 --> 00:13:58,119
by burying their endings.

272
00:13:58,119 --> 00:13:59,619
What?

273
00:13:59,619 --> 00:14:00,619
You're the ones responsible for tearing out the story's endings?

274
00:14:00,619 --> 00:14:01,619
Come.

